,title,link,text,language,family
0,Tiwi people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiwi_people,"1 month ago - The Tiwi language is a language ... Australians beyond recent linguistic interaction as a result of the federal government's Stolen Generations relocation policies. Tiwi society is based on matrilineal descent, and marriage plays a very important part in many aspects of their lives. Art and music form an intrinsic ...",Tiwi,Australian
1,Songs of the Tiwi: Traditional Aboriginal Music of AustraliaTiwi people - WikipediaTiwi Islands — Ngarakuruwala (We Sing) Group: Tiwi Cultural ...The Old Songs are Always New – Sydney University PressThe Old Songs are Always New - Sydney Open LibraryUndercover Music,http://www.manikay.com/albums/tiwi.shtml,"A searchable discography of traditional Aboriginal music from Arnhem Land. Includes sound files, cover photos, liner notes and more! Some of these songs have been recorded and archived and some performances by Tiwi women have been held at a number of important venues in Australia. The Tiwi ""strong women's group"" are involved in a collaborative project to conserve their music on Bathurst and Melville islands. Jan 21, 2026 · Every Tiwi song carries a story — a living tradition that reflects the Tiwi way of life, culture, and heritage. These songs are more than music; they are a vital part of the Tiwi... The Old Songs are Always New explores the return home of these recordings to the Tiwi Islands and describes the musical and vocal characteristics, performance context and cultural function of the twelve Tiwi song types, giving an overview of the linguistic and poetic devices used by Tiwi composers. The Old Songs are Always New explores their return home to the Tiwi Islands and reveals that the fundamentally contemporary, topical and current nature of the Tiwi song culture has resulted in the preservation of a rich social, cultural and historical oral record. Tiwi songs are items of significant Australian musical heritage that we should all be proud of. Since 2007, as Ngarukuruwala (we sing songs), the Tiwi Strong Women’s Group and musicians from down south have shared musical ideas to create new versions of old Tiwi songs.",Tiwi,Australian
2,Nyngawi – Tiwi Traditional Song | Performed by Ngarakuruwala ...Songs of the Tiwi: Traditional Aboriginal Music of AustraliaTiwi people - WikipediaTiwi Islands — Ngarakuruwala (We Sing) Group: Tiwi Cultural ...The Old Songs are Always New – Sydney University PressThe Old Songs are Always New - Sydney Open LibraryUndercover Music,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-vDjvynynBc,"Feb 5, 2026 · This song speaks of Nyngawi, a well-known figure in Tiwi oral tradition. Nyngawi is often described as a hairy man of the bush, living deep within the forest and mangrove areas. A searchable discography of traditional Aboriginal music from Arnhem Land. Includes sound files, cover photos, liner notes and more! Some of these songs have been recorded and archived and some performances by Tiwi women have been held at a number of important venues in Australia. The Tiwi ""strong women's group"" are involved in a collaborative project to conserve their music on Bathurst and Melville islands. Jan 21, 2026 · Every Tiwi song carries a story — a living tradition that reflects the Tiwi way of life, culture, and heritage. These songs are more than music; they are a vital part of the Tiwi... The Old Songs are Always New explores the return home of these recordings to the Tiwi Islands and describes the musical and vocal characteristics, performance context and cultural function of the twelve Tiwi song types, giving an overview of the linguistic and poetic devices used by Tiwi composers. The Old Songs are Always New explores their return home to the Tiwi Islands and reveals that the fundamentally contemporary, topical and current nature of the Tiwi song culture has resulted in the preservation of a rich social, cultural and historical oral record. Tiwi songs are items of significant Australian musical heritage that we should all be proud of. Since 2007, as Ngarukuruwala (we sing songs), the Tiwi Strong Women’s Group and musicians from down south have shared musical ideas to create new versions of old Tiwi songs.",Tiwi,Australian
3,Tiwi Islands — Ngarakuruwala (We Sing) Group: Tiwi Cultural ...The Old Songs are Always New – Sydney University PressThe Old Songs are Always New - Sydney Open LibraryUndercover Music,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BbqfwklDoLo,"Jan 21, 2026 · Every Tiwi song carries a story — a living tradition that reflects the Tiwi way of life, culture, and heritage. These songs are more than music; they are a vital part of the Tiwi... The Old Songs are Always New explores the return home of these recordings to the Tiwi Islands and describes the musical and vocal characteristics, performance context and cultural function of the twelve Tiwi song types, giving an overview of the linguistic and poetic devices used by Tiwi composers. The Old Songs are Always New explores their return home to the Tiwi Islands and reveals that the fundamentally contemporary, topical and current nature of the Tiwi song culture has resulted in the preservation of a rich social, cultural and historical oral record. Tiwi songs are items of significant Australian musical heritage that we should all be proud of. Since 2007, as Ngarukuruwala (we sing songs), the Tiwi Strong Women’s Group and musicians from down south have shared musical ideas to create new versions of old Tiwi songs.",Tiwi,Australian
4,Undercover Music,https://undercovermusic.com.au/ngarukuruwala.htm,"Tiwi songs are items of significant Australian musical heritage that we should all be proud of. Since 2007, as Ngarukuruwala (we sing songs), the Tiwi Strong Women’s Group and musicians from down south have shared musical ideas to create new versions of old Tiwi songs.",Tiwi,Australian
5,Tiwi Music - Behind The News,https://www.abc.net.au/btn/classroom/tiwi-music/10536664,"December 9, 2019 - The Tiwi people have lived here for centuries. But traditionally, Indigenous Australian's didn't write down their history. Instead stories were passed down from generation to generation through story-telling, songs and dances. Geneveive Campbell is a Sydney musician who's come to collect those those musical stories so they can be shared and preserved forever.",Tiwi,Australian
6,BTN: Tiwi music: Keeping an ancient culture alive - ABC Education,https://www.abc.net.au/education/btn-tiwi-music-keeping-the-ancient-culture-alive/13592826,"October 19, 2021 - A group of Tiwis sit on the ground, singing in their local language. The camera pans away to show a white woman accompanying the singers on a French horn. ... Genevieve Campbell is a musician and she's here to collect those stories so they can be shared and preserved forever.",Tiwi,Australian
7,The Sounds of Tiwi | Off The Leash,https://offtheleash.net.au/features/music/2020/02/sounds-tiwi,"February 26, 2020 - Ngarukuruwala is the name of the collaboration that has been uniting the incredible culture, stories, and songs of the Tiwi women with Sydney-based musicians for over a decade.",Tiwi,Australian
8,Australian Indigenous Resources - Music & Performing Arts - Subject Guides at Western Sydney University,https://subjectguides.library.westernsydney.edu.au/performingartsmusic/indigenous_music,"The songs presented in this book ... years of Tiwi storytelling, ceremony and in the songlines that circle the islands. As custodians of the songs, the Ngarukuruwala Women’s Group in partnership with Dr Genevieve Campbell have recorded over 40 songs in language for the first time. ... Decolonising and Indigenising Music Education ...",Tiwi,Australian
9,"Tiwi people - Alchetron, The Free Social Encyclopedia",https://alchetron.com/Tiwi-people,"February 13, 2026 - The Tiwi people are one of the many Indigenous groups of Australia. Nearly 2,500 Tiwi live in the Bathurst and Melville Islands, which make up the Tiwi Islands. The Tiwi Islanders are famous for their great musicians, art and sports players. Notable Tiwi people include David Kantilla, Austin Wonaeamirri and Adam Kerinaua.",Tiwi,Australian
